.vscode/**
src/**
scripts/**

# Commit hooks, pointed at by core.hooksPath. Repo machinery, not runtime.
.githooks/**

# The release workflow. Same reasoning, and the allow-list caught it shipping.
.github/**
node_modules/**
tsconfig.json

# `*.map` alone matches only the root; source maps live in out/ and nearly
# doubled the payload before this.
**/*.map

# Fixtures carry quota snapshots from a real account. Redacted, but there is
# no reason to distribute them.
test/**

# Contributor and agent documentation. The README is the Marketplace page and
# its relative links resolve against the repository.
docs/**
CLAUDE.md
.gitignore

# The icon source, kept in the repo for regeneration but not shipped.
images/*.svg
# ...but the activity-bar container names this one, and a container with no
# icon renders as a blank strip. Preflight proves every icon the manifest
# points at is actually in the package, having once caught this exact thing.
# The activity-bar glyph, which the manifest names. icon.svg stays behind: it
# is the source drawing for icon.png and nothing loads it at runtime, which
# preflight proves by refusing any image the manifest does not point at.
!images/activity.svg

# Screenshots are referenced from the repository by absolute URL (vsce rewrites
# them), so shipping copies inside the package is dead weight. The icon stays:
# it is loaded from the manifest.
# Every png but the icon. The rule named Screen-*.png, so the first screenshot
# with a different name shipped inside the package -- which the allow-list
# caught, being the fourth thing it has caught that this file had not been told
# about yet.
images/*.png
!images/icon.png

# Rendered previews, written by scripts/preview.mjs.
.preview/**
